# Force LF on checkout for every text file, regardless of a contributor's
# local core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a fresh clone/checkout on a
# machine with core.autocrlf=true silently rewrites CRLF into any migration
# file containing a multi-line dollar-quoted PL/pgSQL body (e.g.
# packages/database/migrations/0030_add_integrity_triggers.sql) — the CRLF
# bytes land verbatim inside the stored function definition, which is
# byte-identical to Postgres but not to a deterministic schema fingerprint.
# Found and fixed during DB6-S27's clean-clone rehearsal.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
